#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bec12e1c-bc47-5ac1-a1aa-f9de136b90cd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Appropriate Units of Area and Volume"}] :question/id #uuid "6cbff12b-cc20-5db4-9e64-8bb7b4c62dd9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10149" :question/problem "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a shoe box. What units could we use?\n\n1. $\\textrm{cm}^2$\n2. $\\textrm{cm}^3$\n3. $\\textrm{kg}$" :question/worked-solution "We can measure length in centimeters $(\\textrm{cm})$. When measuring lengths in centimeters, volumes are measured in $\\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm}$, which is usually written as $\\textrm{cm}^3$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188008 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188301 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "469f0c76-3641-5a56-82bb-9ac807ff2017" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Volume With the Correct Units"}] :question/id #uuid "94639d5a-c922-52f3-8e50-82d0e9a3dbad" :question/math-academy-id "e-10150" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7e21a9afeb5a6c102a8426255b17112479144845be87f121435c8e27078610ab.png)\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube shown in the diagram above?" :question/worked-solution "To find the volume $V$ of a cube, we cube its side length. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= (5m)^{3} \\\\\n&= 5m \\cdot 5m \\cdot 5m \\\\\n&= (5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5) \\cdot (m \\cdot m \\cdot m) \\\\\n&= 125m^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188302 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09b56d66-4e96-56de-b3fa-747cb2e3487d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Area With the Correct Units"}] :question/id #uuid "5f153b4a-2706-5ff6-b0b3-65cfc29e1391" :question/math-academy-id "e-10163" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7e300a90dbfda5a9210cec502c2879b7950e2765c433eb6ee6284e74db3cd220.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the square above?" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= (5ft)^{2} \\\\\n&= 5ft \\cdot 5ft \\\\\n&= (5 \\cdot 5) \\cdot (ft \\cdot ft) \\\\\n&= 25ft^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bec12e1c-bc47-5ac1-a1aa-f9de136b90cd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Appropriate Units of Area and Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99d9038b-79fb-5c91-94bb-fcd7806af560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185701} {:answer/id #uuid "baa7dce1-c607-56ec-b3e4-ccc2fa51f78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185702} {:answer/id #uuid "e62a0192-4d50-54d4-b820-0939c7757773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "in" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185703} {:answer/id #uuid "086f7fdc-467e-5e35-852f-6f65df0bf70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "in^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185704} {:answer/id #uuid "14687508-0774-5f65-be72-954b9bbb19a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185705}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8b08e998-197e-5fff-8659-5d89e0f6dcbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185700}] :question/id #uuid "466efffd-5b60-5120-9dd7-a526b8962ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-144091" :question/problem "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a fish tank. What units could we use?"}]}
